{"source": "Sefaria, Jastrow entries opened by page name (not returned by the word search)", "fetched": "2026-10-22", "queries": {}, "entries": {"B00002": {"headword": "ב׳", "rid": "B00002", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " as a numeral letter, <i>two;</i> v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_א׳.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, א׳ 1\">א׳</a>."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "E00433": {"headword": "הימני׳", "rid": "E00433", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " , <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Eruvin.94a\" data-ref=\"Eruvin 94a\">Erub. 94ᵃ</a>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_הִמְיָינָא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, הִמְיָינָא 1\">הֶמְיָינָא</a>"}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "G00527": {"headword": "זְמַם I", "rid": "G00527", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_זָמַם I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, זָמַם I 1\">same</a>."}, {"definition": " <b>Af.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אַזֵּים</span></b>  = <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_זָמַם I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, זָמַם I 1\">preced.</a> <i>Hif.</i> <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Deuteronomy.19.18\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Deuteronomy 19:18\">Targ. Y. Deut. XIX, 18</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">דמַזְמִין</span> who rebut.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Kamma.73b.16\" data-ref=\"Bava Kamma 73b:16\">B. Kam. 73ᵇ</a> bot. <span dir=\"rtl\">דאפכינהו ואַזְמִינְהוּ</span> they reversed their statement of the case and also testified to an alibi as to time and place."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִיתַּזֵּים</span></b>, <b><span dir=\"rtl\"> אִיתַּזַּם</span></b> <i>to be proven a false witness</i>. Ib. 73ᵃ <span dir=\"rtl\">כי מִתַּזְּמֵי אטביחה</span> when they were proven false witnesses with reference to slaughtering; <span dir=\"rtl\">ואִיתַּזְּמוּ להו אגניבה</span> and they are considered as false witnesses also with reference to stealing. Ib. <span dir=\"rtl\">אטביחה דקא מִיתַּזְּמֵי אִיתַּזּוּם</span> as regards the testimony to slaughtering on which they were refuted, they are refuted; a. e.—<i>Ithpe.</i> <span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְּזוֹם</span>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Makkot.3b\" data-ref=\"Makkot 3b\">Macc. 3ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳ חד מינייהו</span> against one of them an alibi was proven."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "G00643": {"headword": "זְקַן", "rid": "G00643", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_זָקֵן I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, זָקֵן I 1\">same</a>."}, {"definition": " <b>Af.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אַזְקֵן</span></b> <b>1)</b> <i>to make old, weaken</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Eruvin.56a\" data-ref=\"Eruvin 56a\">Erub. 56ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">הני מולייתא אַזְקְנוּן …</span> those ascents … made us (me) old, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_בֵּירַאי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, בֵּירַאי 1\">בֵּירַאי</a>. <b>—2)</b> <i>to grow old</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Niddah.47a\" data-ref=\"Niddah 47a\">Nidd. 47ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אַזְקְנָא לה</span> (some ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">אזקונא</span>, Asheri <span dir=\"rtl\">אזקנה</span>) this would be a sign that she has entered old age (passed the change of life)."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "I00676": {"headword": "טְפַף", "rid": "I00676", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_טָפַף II.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, טָפַף II 1\">same</a>."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִיטַּף</span></b> <i>to be dripped</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Job.15.8\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Job 15:8\">Targ. Job XV, 8</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ואִיטַּפַּת</span> (some ed. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_טְפֵי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, טְפֵי 1\">אַטְפֵי</a>, h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">תגרע</span>, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גָּרַע II.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גָּרַע II 1\"><span dir=\"rtl\">גָּרַע</span> II</a>)."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "K00107": {"headword": "כִּדְ׳ כַּדְבוּבָא", "rid": "K00107", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " m.  (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_כַּדְבֵּב.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, כַּדְבֵּב 1\">preced.</a>) <i>falsehood, lie; fiction</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Job.16.8\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Job 16:8\">Targ. Job XVI, 8</a>.—Pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּדְבוּבִין</span>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Job.11.3\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Job 11:3\">Ib. XI, 3</a>."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "L00001": {"headword": "ל׳", "rid": "L00001", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " , as a numeral letter, <i>thirty</i>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_א׳.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, א׳ 1\">א׳</a>."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "M02444": {"headword": "מְקַק", "rid": "M02444", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_מָקַק.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, מָקַק 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpalp.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְמַקְמֵק</span></b> <b>1)</b> <i>to pine away, be weakened</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Deuteronomy.31.18\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Deuteronomy 31:18\">Targ. Y. Deut. XXXI, 18</a>; a. e. <b>—2)</b> <i>to decay, melt</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Job.14.10\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Job 14:10\">Targ. Job XIV, 10</a> (h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">חלש</span>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Psalms.73.8\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Psalms 73:8\">Targ. Ps. LXXIII, 8</a> (h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">ימיקו</span>). <b>—3)</b> <i>to sneeze</i>, v. infra."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpe.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִיתְמְקַק</span></b>  (cmp. <span dir=\"rtl\">מוג</span>, <i>Ithpol</i>.)  <b>1)</b> <i>to be languid, to stretch one’s self</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_I_Kings.17.21\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on I Kings 17:21\">Targ. I Kings XVII, 21</a>. <b>—2)</b>  [<i>to collapse</i>; v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_מַרְפֵּא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, מַרְפֵּא 1\">מַרְפֵּא</a> a. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עָטַשׁ.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עָטַשׁ 1\">עָטַשׁ</a>,] <i>to sneeze</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_II_Kings.4.35\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on II Kings 4:35\">Targ. II Kings IV, 35</a> ed. Lag. (ed. Ven. I אִתְמוֹקַק <i>Ithpol</i>. of <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_מוּק.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, מוּק 1\">מוּק</a>; Regia <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_מְקַק.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, מְקַק 1\">אִתְמַקְמַק</a>; ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">אתמורק</span>; h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">ויזורר</span>; Pesh. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_פְּקַק.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, פְּקַק 1\">אתפקק</a>)."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "M02697": {"headword": "מְרַךְ", "rid": "M02697", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_מָרַךְ.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, מָרַךְ 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Itphe.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְמְרִיךְ</span></b>  (cmp. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_מוֹרֶךְ.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, מוֹרֶךְ 1\">מוֹרֶךְ</a>) <i>to be faint, become unsteady</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Onkelos_Deuteronomy.19.5\" data-ref=\"Onkelos Deuteronomy 19:5\">Targ. O. Deut. XIX, 5</a> ed. Berl., v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_מְרַג.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, מְרַג 1\">מְרַג</a>."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "M03049": {"headword": "מתיב", "rid": "M03049", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " , <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Genesis.4.8\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Genesis 4:8\">Targ. Y. I Gen. IV, 8</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ אפין</span>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_מִיסַּב.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, מִיסַּב 1\">מִיסַּב</a>"}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "P00766": {"headword": "עֲלַב", "rid": "P00766", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עָלַב.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עָלַב 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְעַלֵּב</span></b>, <b></b>"}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpe.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְעֲלֵב</span></b> <b>1)</b> <i>to humble one’s self, submit</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_I_Kings.12.7\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on I Kings 12:7\">Targ. I Kings XII, 7</a> (h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">תהיה עבד</span>). <b>—2)</b>  (v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עוּלְבַּן.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עוּלְבַּן 1\">עוּלְבַּן</a>) <i>to raise one’s self above; to jest, sneer at</i> (= h. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עָלַל.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עָלַל 1\">התעלל</a>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Judges.19.25\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Judges 19:25\">Targ. Jud. XIX, 25</a> ed. Lag., v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_לְעַב.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, לְעַב 1\">לְעַב</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_I_Samuel.31.4\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on I Samuel 31:4\">Targ. I Sam. XXXI, 4</a> ed. Lag. (oth. ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">יתלעב׳</span>) <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Jeremiah.38.19\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Jeremiah 38:19\">Targ. Jer. XXXVIII, 19</a> ed. Lag. (oth. ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">יתלעב׳</span>).—[<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_of_II_Chronicles.30.10\" data-ref=\"Targum of II Chronicles 30:10\">Targ. II Chr. XXX, 10</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_of_II_Chronicles.36.16\" data-ref=\"Targum of II Chronicles 36:16\">XXXVI, 16</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מתעלב׳</span> ed. Bxt. (oth. ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">מתלעב׳</span>).]"}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "P00918": {"headword": "עֲמַק", "rid": "P00918", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עָמַק.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עָמַק 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Af.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אַעֲמִיק</span></b> <i>to grow deeper</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Isaiah.30.33\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Isaiah 30:33\">Targ. Is. XXX, 33</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לאַעֲמָקָא</span> ed. Lag. (ed. Wil. <span dir=\"rtl\">לַעֲמִיקָא</span> = <span dir=\"rtl\">לְאַעֲ׳</span>; oth. ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">לעַמָּקָא</span>, <i>Pa.</i>), v. preced.—[<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Proverbs.28.6\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Proverbs 28:6\">Targ. Prov. XXVIII, 6</a> דמעמיק מן Var. ed. Lag., v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עֲקַם.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עֲקַם 1\">עֲקם</a>.]"}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "P01210": {"headword": "עֲקַף", "rid": "P01210", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עָקַף.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עָקַף 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpe.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְעֲקַף</span></b> <i>to seek occasion against</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Genesis.43.18\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Genesis 43:18\">Targ. Y. Gen. XLIII, 18</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">למִתְעַקְפָא</span> (<i>infin</i>.; O. <span dir=\"rtl\">לאסתקפא</span>, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_סְקַף I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, סְקַף I 1\"><span dir=\"rtl\">סְקַף</span> I</a>)."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "Q00078": {"headword": "פִּגְמִין", "rid": "Q00078", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " m."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "Q02043": {"headword": "פְּרַת I", "rid": "Q02043", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_פָּרַת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, פָּרַת 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Pa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">פָּרֵית</span></b> <b>1)</b> <i>to divide, dismember</i> (of the basilisk whose look is believed to cause a person’s limbs to fall apart, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עֶכֶס.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עֶכֶס 1\">עֶכֶס</a>, a. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.10\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 10\">Gen. R. s. 10</a>, a. e., quot. s. v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_נָשַׁל.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, נָשַׁל 1\">נָשַׁל</a>; cmp. <span dir=\"rtl\">יַפְרִישׁ</span> <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Proverbs.23.32\" data-ref=\"Proverbs 23:32\">Prov. XXIII, 32</a>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Isaiah.14.29\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Isaiah 14:29\">Targ. Is. XIV, 29</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מְפָרֵית</span> (some ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַפְרִית</span> <i>Af</i>.; Var. ed. Lag. <span dir=\"rtl\">מפריד</span>; ed. Wil. <span dir=\"rtl\">מפריח</span>; h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">פעופף</span>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Isaiah.59.5\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Isaiah 59:5\">Ib. LIX, 5</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מְפָרְתִין</span> ed. Lag. (ed. Wil. <span dir=\"rtl\">מפרחין</span>).—[<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Proverbs.23.32\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Proverbs 23:32\">Targ. Prov. XXIII, 32</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">דפריח</span>, ed. Lag. <span dir=\"rtl\">פאריח</span>, prob. to be read: <span dir=\"rtl\">דפָרֵית</span>, Part. <i>Pe</i>.; h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">יפריש</span>, v. supra.] <b>—2)</b> <i>to belittle, make light of</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Eichah_Rabbah,_Petichta.7\" data-ref=\"Eichah Rabbah, Petichta 7\">Lam. R. to II, 10</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">הוון חמשא … ומְפָרְתִין ליה בנבוכדנצר וכ׳</span> (read: <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_בִּיָּא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, בִּיָּא 1\">ביה</a>; Ar. <span dir=\"rtl\">ופרטין</span>) five kings were sitting and sneering at Nebuchadnezzar in the presence of Zedekiah; <span dir=\"rtl\">אף הוא מְפָרְתֵיה לנב׳ וכ׳</span> (Ar. <span dir=\"rtl\">פרטיה</span>, Var. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_פדרת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, פדרת 1\">פדרת</a>, corr. acc.) he, likewise, sneered &c."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpe.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִיפְּרַת</span></b> <i>to be broken off, separated</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Beitzah.2a.3\" data-ref=\"Beitzah 2a:3\">Bets. 2ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אוכלא דאִפְּרַת היא</span> the egg is considered as a broken-off piece of food (part of the hen, not as an independent creation). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pesachim.85a.14\" data-ref=\"Pesachim 85a:14\">Pes. 85ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">כמאן דמִפַּרְתֵי דמי</span> they are to be considered as if they were separated; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Chullin.73a\" data-ref=\"Chullin 73a\">Ḥull. 73ᵃ</a>"}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "R00217": {"headword": "צוּף", "rid": "R00217", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_צוּף.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, צוּף 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpe.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִצְטַיֵּיף</span></b> <i>to look out</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jerusalem,_Numbers.21.20\" data-ref=\"Targum Jerusalem, Numbers 21:20\">Targ. Y. II, Num. XXI, 20</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">דמִצְטַיְּיפָא</span> (Bxt. <span dir=\"rtl\">דמִצְטַפְיָיא</span>; Targ. O. <span dir=\"rtl\">ומסטבייא</span>; h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">ונשקפה</span>)."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "S00733": {"headword": "קְטַט", "rid": "S00733", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_קָטַט.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, קָטַט 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Af.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אָקֵיט</span></b>  (cmp. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_צָעַר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, צָעַר 1\">צָעַר</a>) <i>to vex, annoy</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Metzia.61b.2\" data-ref=\"Bava Metzia 61b:2\">B. Mets. 61ᵇ</a> (in Hebrew diction) <span dir=\"rtl\">לא תגנב על מנת למֵיקַט</span> (some ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">למֵקַט</span>; Ms. M. <span dir=\"rtl\">למקט׳</span>, corr. acc.) ‘thou shalt not steal (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Exodus.20.15\" data-ref=\"Exodus 20:15\">Ex. XX, 15</a>), not even if it be only with the intention of vexing (thy neighbor, until thou restore the stolen object); <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Tosefta_Bava_Kamma.10.37\" data-ref=\"Tosefta Bava Kamma 10:37\">Tosef. B. Kam. X, 37</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Yalkut_Shimoni_on_Torah.605\" data-ref=\"Yalkut Shimoni on Torah 605\">Yalk. Lev. 605</a>; Sifra Ḳ’dosh. ch. III, Par. 2; Y. Snh. X, beg. 30ᵃ"}, {"definition": " <b>Pa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">קַטֵּיט</span></b>  [<i>to thin</i>,], (music) <i>to produce a fine</i> (<i>high</i>) <i>sound, to sing tenor</i> or <i>soprano</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Arakhin.13b.55\" data-ref=\"Arakhin 13b:55\">Arakh. 13ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">הני מְקַטְּטֵי וכ׳</span> they (the young Levites) sang high, and they (the older Levites) could not do it."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpe.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִיקַּט</span></b>  (v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_קְטָטָה.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, קְטָטָה 1\">next w.</a>) <i>to quarrel</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Niddah.67b.36\" data-ref=\"Niddah 67b:36\">Nidd. 67ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לאו הכי הוה עובדא … דאִיקּוּט וכ׳</span> was it not so with the wife of Abba Mari … when they had a quarrel, and R. N. went &c.?"}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpol.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְקוֹטַט</span></b>  (fr. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_קוּט.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, קוּט 1\">קוּט</a>) same. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Leviticus.24.10\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Leviticus 24:10\">Targ. Y. Lev. XXIV, 10</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Lamentations.4.15\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Lamentations 4:15\">Targ. Lam. IV, 15</a>."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "S02268": {"headword": "קְשַׁשׁ I", "rid": "S02268", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_קָשַׁשׁ II.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, קָשַׁשׁ II 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Polel.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">קוֹשֵׁשׁ</span></b> <i>to straighten, correct</i>, v. infra."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpolel.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְקוֹשֵׁשׁ</span></b> <i>to correct one’s self</i>. Y. Taan. II, 65ᵃ bot. (ref. to <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Zephaniah.2.1\" data-ref=\"Zephaniah 2:1\">Zeph. II, 1</a>) <span dir=\"rtl\">נִתְקוֹשֵׁשׁ גרמן עד דלא נְקוֹשֵׁשׁ חורנין</span> let us correct ourselves before we correct others; v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_קָשַׁט.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, קָשַׁט 1\">קָשַׁט</a>"}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "T00146": {"headword": "רַבְרֵב", "rid": "T00146", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_רִבְרֵב.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, רִבְרֵב 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְרַבְרֵב</span></b> <b>1)</b> <i>to be chief; to lead; to be great</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_of_I_Chronicles.15.22\" data-ref=\"Targum of I Chronicles 15:22\">Targ. I Chr. XV, 22</a> (h. text <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יָסַר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יָסַר 1\">יָסֹר</a>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Job.33.12\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Job 33:12\">Targ. Job XXXIII, 12</a> (Ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְרָרַב</span>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Proverbs.8.16\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Proverbs 8:16\">Targ. Prov. VIII, 16</a> (Ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְרוֹרְבְיָין</span>); a. e. <b>—2)</b> <i>to claim superiority; to boast</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Onkelos_Numbers.16.3\" data-ref=\"Onkelos Numbers 16:3\">Targ. Num. XVI, 3</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Onkelos_Numbers.16.13\" data-ref=\"Onkelos Numbers 16:13\">13</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Ezekiel.5.15\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Ezekiel 5:15\">Targ. Ez. V, 15</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Genesis.14.23\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Genesis 14:23\">Targ. Y. Gen. XIV, 23</a>. Targ. II Esth. VIII, 13 (ed. Lag. <span dir=\"rtl\">נִתְרוֹרֵב</span>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Jeremiah.48.42\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Jeremiah 48:42\">Targ. Jer. XLVIII, 42</a> (ed. Lag. <span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְרָרְבוּ</span>); a. fr.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.89\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 89\">Gen. R. s. 89</a>, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_רַבְרְבָא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, רַבְרְבָא 1\">next w.</a>"}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "T00773": {"headword": "רְכַס", "rid": "T00773", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_רָכַס.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, רָכַס 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpe.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִירְכַס</span></b>  [<i>to be trodden on</i>,] <i>to be lost</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Batra.14b.9\" data-ref=\"Bava Batra 14b:9\">B. Bath. 14ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">איידי דזוטר מִירְכִיס</span> because it (the Book of Hosea) is small, it might have been lost (if circulated as a separate book). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Ketubot.57a\" data-ref=\"Ketubot 57a\">Keth. 57ᵃ</a> top <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳ כתובתה</span> (sub. <span dir=\"rtl\">שטר</span>) her marriage deed was lost. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Yevamot.113b.16\" data-ref=\"Yevamot 113b:16\">Yeb. 113ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אִירְכְּסוּ ליה מפתחי וכ׳</span> (not <span dir=\"rtl\">מפתח</span>) had lost the keys of the college building; a. e."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "T00942": {"headword": "רְפַט", "rid": "T00942", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_רָפַט.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, רָפַט 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpe.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִירְפַּט</span></b> <i>to fall apart</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Megillah.26b\" data-ref=\"Megillah 26b\">Meg. 26ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\">האי תיבותא</span> (<a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_רַבָּתִי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, רַבָּתִי 1\">רבתי</a>) <span dir=\"rtl\">דאירפט וכ׳</span></span> (read: <span dir=\"rtl\">דאִירְפְּטָא</span>; Ms. M. 2 <span dir=\"rtl\">דאיפרט</span>, v. Rabb. D. S. a. l. note 3) a large chest (for sacred scrolls) which has fallen apart, may be made over into a small one."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "T00958": {"headword": "רְפַף", "rid": "T00958", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_רָפַף.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, רָפַף 1\">same</a>"}, {"definition": " <b>Pa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">רַפֵּיף</span></b> <i>to shake</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Genesis.44.18\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Genesis 44:18\">Targ. Y. Gen. XLIV, 18</a> addit. (at the end of Gen. in ed. pr., at the end of Ex. in ed. Lsb.) <span dir=\"rtl\">בעט יוסף בעמודא דהיכלא ורַפְּפֵיה</span> Joseph struck with his foot a column of the palace and made it tremble."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִתְרַפּף</span></b> <i>to be shaken, tremble</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Job.9.6\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Job 9:6\">Targ. Job IX, 6</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מִתְרַפְּפִין</span> (ed. Wil. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִתְרוֹפְפִין</span>, <i>Ithpol.</i>; h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">יתפלצון</span>)."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "U00208": {"headword": "שְׂגַב", "rid": "U00208", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch.  <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_שָׂגַב.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, שָׂגַב 1\">same</a>."}, {"definition": " <b>Pa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">שַׂגֵּיב</span></b> <i>to elevate, lift up, strengthen</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Psalms.20.2\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Psalms 20:2\">Targ. Ps. XX, 2</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Psalms.91.14\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Psalms 91:14\">Ib. XCI, 14</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Proverbs.4.6\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Proverbs 4:6\">Targ. Prov. IV, 6</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּתְשַׂגְּבִינָךְ</span> ed. Lag. (ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּתֻשְׂגָּבְיָךְ</span>; oth. ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">וּתְשׂוֹגְבִינָךְ</span>); a. e."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "U01492": {"headword": "שְׁמַם", "rid": "U01492", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch.  <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_שָׁמֵם.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, שָׁמֵם 1\">same</a>."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִשְׁתְּמַם</span></b> <b>1)</b> <i>to be desolate</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Aramaic_Targum_to_Lamentations.4.5\" data-ref=\"Aramaic Targum to Lamentations 4:5\">Targ. Lam. IV, 5</a>. <b>—2)</b> <i>to be confounded, mad</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_I_Samuel.21.14\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on I Samuel 21:14\">Targ. I Sam. XXI, 14</a> (h. text <span dir=\"rtl\">ויתהלל</span>)."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpol.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִשְׁתּוֹמֵם</span></b> <i>to be perplexed</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Chullin.21a.2\" data-ref=\"Chullin 21a:2\">Ḥull. 21ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳ כשעה חדא</span> (fr. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Daniel.4.16\" data-ref=\"Daniel 4:16\">Dan. IV, 16</a>) he was perplexed for a moment (knew not what to answer)."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "U01497": {"headword": "שְׁמֵן", "rid": "U01497", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch.  <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_שָׁמֵן I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, שָׁמֵן I 1\">same</a>."}, {"definition": " <b>Ithpa.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אִשְׁתַּמֵּן</span></b> <i>to grow fat</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.28\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 28\">Gen. R. s. 28</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אמר ליה זיל ואש׳ … ומִשְׁתַּמֵּן וכ׳</span> he said to the bird, go and grow fat, and come again, and it went and grew fat, and came again; Yalk. Zeph. 566."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "U01626": {"headword": "שׁע׳", "rid": "U01626", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " pr. n. m., v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_*שִׁשְׁעָה.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, *שִׁשְׁעָה 1\">שִׁשְׁעָה</a>"}]}, "alt_headwords": []}, "V00774": {"headword": "תְּעֵב", "rid": "V00774", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " ch.  <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_תָּעַב.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, תָּעַב 1\">same</a>."}, {"definition": " <b>Af.</b> - <b><span dir=\"rtl\">אַתְעֵב</span></b> <i>to act abominably</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Ezekiel.16.52\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Ezekiel 16:52\">Targ. Ez. XVI, 52</a>."}]}, "alt_headwords": []}}}